# Module conventions

A module is `internal/app/<module>`. Layout:

```
<module>/
  README.md        what it owns, its surface, its tables
  gqlgen.yml       when it is a GraphQL subgraph
  auth/            directives for GraphQL, the same checks as gin middleware for REST
  model/           GORM structs embedding a core-lib base model
  dto/             service-facing types; Create*/Update* requests (pointers = patch semantics)
  repository/      SQL only; table constant, namespace filter, soft delete, RepositoryError
  service/         validation, enum checks, list allow-lists, business rules
  mapper/          dto <-> model with copier (CopyWithOption is swappable in tests)
  graphql/         schema/, generated/ (never edit), resolver/ (thin), mapper/ (gql <-> dto), loader/
  rest/            router.go (Register + error mapping), <entity>_controller.go
```

Rules:

- Resolvers and controllers only translate and call the service.
- The service validates every input it receives, including list filters and sorts.
- Repositories never trust the caller's namespace; they read it from the context.
- Factories hand out singletons through `sync.Once`; constructors take no arguments.
- Logging uses `logger.GetLogger()` with messages `<Module>.<Entity>.<Layer>.<Method>.Error`.
- Each GraphQL module carries its own copy of the shared schema files (directive, enum, filter, page,
  sort, scalar) so each subgraph composes on its own.
